{"name":"Yellow Tang","hex":"#ffd300","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow tang","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Zebrasoma flavescens, a species of bright yellow saltwater ray-finned fish in the family Acanthuridae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow_tang"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yellow tang","blocks":[{"text":"The yellow tang, also known as the lemon sailfin, yellow sailfin tang or somber surgeonfish, is a species of marine ray-finned fish belonging to the family Acanthuridae which includes the surgeonfishes, unicornfishes and tangs. Bright yellow in color, this Pacific reef fish is also one of the most popular marine aquarium fish. The yellow tang spawns around a full moon, eats algae, and has a white barb located just before the tail fin to protect itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Zebrasoma_flavescens_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_tang"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg/500px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg/1280px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg/500px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"With fins fully extended","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZebrasoma_flavescens_2589.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Yellow_Tangs_%28109517014%29.jpg/500px-Yellow_Tangs_%28109517014%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Yellow_Tangs_%28109517014%29.jpg/500px-Yellow_Tangs_%28109517014%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In Maui","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellow_Tangs_(109517014).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG/500px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG/1280px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG/500px-Zebrasoma_flavescens_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"At the State Museum of Natural History